1. Aim
To develop a Python program that reads machine log files, processes data using regular expressions, handles invalid records and generates production reports.

2. Objectives
IT12: Create a log file containing at least 15 records, including invalid entries.
IT10: Read, parse, validate and generate report and rejects files.
IT8: Use regular expressions (re) to extract and validate log data.
IT6: Process multiple files and generate combined plant reports with run history.
3. Concepts Used
File handling (open, read, write)
File modes (r, w, a)
Regular expressions (re)
Exception handling
Data validation and aggregation
CSV file handling
Date and time using datetime
Relative file paths
4. Working Procedure
Create data/shift_log.txt.
Read machine log records from the file.
Parse and validate each record.
Separate valid and rejected records.
Calculate count, average, minimum and maximum.
Save the production report in data/report.txt.
Save rejected records in data/rejects.csv.
Generate run history for every execution.
5. File Management
shift_log.txt – Input machine data.
report.txt – Production summary.
rejects.csv – Invalid records and rejection reasons.
run_history.csv – Execution history.
6. Inspection and Testing
Check empty input files.
Test missing and incorrect fields.
Verify CSV separators and headers.
Check decimal precision.
Compare written and read-back values.
Test files created by another pair.
7. Result
Successfully studied Python file handling, regular expressions, data validation and report generation using real machine log files.

8. Conclusion
File handling and regular expressions help automate industrial data processing. They convert raw machine logs into reliable production reports and maintain records for future analysis.
